{"text": "Part six. What it means for you. Ed Elson says that for AI stocks, the bubble has already popped. Damodaran is more struck by the rest of the market, which held up as AI and tech fell. He thinks we're closer to the bottom than two months ago, but waiting for the exact bottom, he says, is an exercise in futility. So his advice for people who never bought tech: add some, at better prices than before. Not all your money, and not necessarily Anthropic. The number to watch next is Anthropic's revenue. If it keeps doubling, his trillion dollar story holds. If not, $77 may still be too high. This is his analysis, not financial advice. That was an hour of Prof G Markets in eight minutes. The full episode is linked below. Tell us in the comments which long podcast we should break down next. And for the AI money story, explained every week, subscribe.", "voice": "brian", "model": "eleven_multilingual_v2", "settings": {"stability": 0.4, "similarity_boost": 0.75, "style": 0.3, "speed": 0.9}, "alignment": {"characters": ["P", "a", "r", "t", " ", "s", "i", "x", ".", " ", "W", "h", "a", "t", " ", "i", "t", " ", "m", "e", "a", "n", "s", " ", "f", "o", "r", " ", "y", "o", "u", ".", " ", "E", "d", " ", "E", "l", "s", "o", "n", " ", "s", "a", "y", "s", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "f", "o", "r", " ", "A", "I", " ", "s", "t", "o", "c", "k", "s", ",", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "b", "u", "b", "b", "l", "e", " ", "h", "a", "s", " ", "a", "l", "r", "e", "a", "d", "y", " ", "p", "o", "p", "p", "e", "d", ".", " ", "D", "a", "m", "o", "d", "a", "r", "a", "n", " ", "i", "s", " ", "m", "o", "r", "e", " ", "s", "t", "r", "u", "c", "k", " ", "b", "y", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "r", "e", "s", "t", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "m", "a", "r", "k", "e", "t", ",", " ", "w", "h", "i", "c", "h", " ", "h", "e", "l", "d", " ", "u", "p", " ", "a", "s", " ", "A", "I", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "t", "e", "c", "h", " ", "f", "e", "l", "l", ".", " ", "H", "e", " ", "t", "h", "i", "n", "k", "